---

<Layout
  title="Teaching"
  description="Applied teaching in databases, SQL, Python, business analytics, information systems, digital citizenship, and responsible AI at UAlbany and beyond."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Teaching / Learning by doing</p>
    <h1>
      Make it clear.
      <br />
      <span class="gradient-text">Make it useful.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I help students connect technical skills to meaningful questions in
      business and society, from their first SQL query to a complete product
      research project.
    </p>
  </header>
  <section class="evidence-row" aria-label="Teaching experience">
    <div class="evidence">
      <strong>12</strong>
      <span>Semesters teaching BITM 330 through Fall 2026</span>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence">
      <strong>~600</strong>
      <span>Undergraduates per year in BITM 330</span>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence">
      <strong>4</strong>
      <span>
        Institutions, spanning undergraduate, graduate, and online teaching
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" style="border-top:0">
    <div class="feature-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Interactive courseware</p>
        <h2>Using Data to Drive Business Performance</h2>
        <p>
          My textbook and companion courseware connect databases, SQL,
          analytics, and business intelligence with practical decision-making.
          Interactive exercises, quizzes, and applied examples support both
          classroom and online learning.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a
            class="button button-primary"
            href="https://database-textbook.dimapublishing.com/"
          >
            Explore the courseware ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Building for online learning</p>
        <h3>Flexible delivery. Purposeful practice.</h3>
        <p>
          I lead development of the fully asynchronous BITM 330 for UAlbany’s
          Online BSBA program, aligned with AACSB Assurance of Learning
          standards and CATLOE instructional design practices.
        </p>
        <p>
          My teaching incorporates AI-assisted coding, LLM evaluation, and
          assignments that ask students to explain and assess their results.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Teaching approach</p>
      <h2>
        Build skills.
        <br />
        Build judgment.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I use applied projects to make technical material approachable. Students
        work through databases, analytics, and digital product questions with an
        emphasis on both the process and the reasoning behind their decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the Business Analytics Practicum and graduate Field Study, student
        teams work on real organizational problems. Their work connects
        research, analysis, prototypes, and communication with stakeholders.
      </p>
      <p>
        <span class="marker">
          Knowing how to use a tool is a beginning. Knowing when to trust the
          result is the real lesson.
        </span>
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/projects/">
        Explore advised projects ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Course portfolio</p>
    <h2>Graduate and MBA courses.</h2>
    <ul class="course-list">
      {graduate.map(([code, title, context]) => (
        <li>
          <p class="status-label">{code}</p>
          <strong>{title}</strong>
          <span>{context}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Undergraduate courses.</h2>
    <ul class="course-list">
      {undergraduate.map(([code, title, context]) => (
        <li>
          <p class="status-label">{code || "Database studies"}</p>
          <strong>{title}</strong>
          <span>{context}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Faculty development</p>
        <h2>
          From prompting
          <br />
          to workflows.
        </h2>
        <p class="lede">
          My CCE 2026 session shares practical ways to use AI agents in academic
          work, including working with files, building websites, and reviewing
          changes.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://nimdvir.github.io/cce-2026/">
          Explore the session and examples ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="plain-card">
        <h3>Teaching, workshops, and collaboration</h3>
        <p>
          I welcome conversations about information systems education, AI
          literacy, digital courseware, and practical academic workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:ndvir@albany.edu">
            Get in touch ↗
          </a>
          <a class="button" href={cvUrl}>
            Full teaching history ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
